  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In 1996, near the Brazilian town of Varginha, where witnesses say a live creature was captured and taken to hospital, men in an unmarked vehicle are said to have pulled up at a gas station and warned a man named Carlos de Souza to keep quiet. De Souza tells Michels himself that one of them \"pointed a finger straight in my face\" and said, \"You didn't see anything. You don't know anything.\" James Fox, who has looked into the case, passes on what de Souza told him, but says only that an unmarked vehicle showed up whose occupants knew who de Souza was. If true, someone was moving fast to silence witnesses."
}
